error[Z0401]: a p-value lies between 0 and 1, but `p` is 1.2 in row 5
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:87
  |
2 | frame(g = ["a", "b", "a", "b", "b"], p = [0.01, 0.2, 0.5, 0.3, 1.2]).add(h = p_adjust(p))
  |                                                                                       ^ not a p-value
  |
  = help: `NA` stands for a p-value that is missing; the row is counted in the frame as the verb receives it, after any `where` or `sort` before it

error[Z0401]: a p-value lies between 0 and 1, but `p` is 1.2 in row 5
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:87
  |
2 | frame(g = ["a", "b", "a", "b", "b"], p = [0.01, 0.2, 0.5, 0.3, 1.2]).add(h = p_adjust(p), by: g)
  |                                                                                       ^ not a p-value
  |
  = help: `NA` stands for a p-value that is missing; the row is counted in the frame as the verb receives it, after any `where` or `sort` before it

